WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.993
Assumptions shape how people interpret information.

2
00:00:02.993 --> 00:00:04.500
Sometimes they are accurate.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.043
Sometimes they are outdated, incomplete, or incorrect.

4
00:00:08.043 --> 00:00:14.897
An assumptions check involves identifying the beliefs underlying an assessment and asking whether they remain valid.

5
00:00:14.897 --> 00:00:16.055
What are we assuming?

6
00:00:16.055 --> 00:00:17.272
Why are we assuming it?

7
00:00:17.272 --> 00:00:19.418
What evidence supports those assumptions?

8
00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:23.359
The technique also asks what would happen if an assumption proved false.

9
00:00:23.359 --> 00:00:30.234
That question can reveal fragile reasoning, information gaps, or areas where the assessment needs caveats.

10
00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:33.527
Making assumptions visible improves analytical quality.

11
00:00:33.527 --> 00:00:38.496
It helps teams challenge default thinking without treating every disagreement as personal.
